## K0007 -- a kernel-only builtin (here cpu_hlt, a privileged instruction) in a hosted program.
## command: lume check   (this file shows the diagnostic: the gate runs a copy named .src; K0007_kernel_builtin_in_hosted.fixed.src is the corrected program)
## fix: use the hosted builtin for the job (a hosted process waits with os_sleep_ms), or build the code as a @freestanding kernel
fn idle_once() = cpu_hlt()
print idle_once()
